bilities such as working memory  response inhibition and sustained  attention  the second circuit called the cortico  cerebellar circuit focuses on the  cerebellum and its projections to the  prefrontal cortex singular gyrus and  some parietal regions this circuit is  involved with analyzing information  about the temporal structure of the  environment  damage to the Circuit would result in  errors related to time estimation  such as how long we think it is going to  take us to do something and perception  the third circuit involves connections  between the ventral portion of the  striatum and the basal ganglia system  and the orbital frontal cortex in the  frontal lobes  it's believed that damage to this  circuit is associated with an inversion  to delayed reinforcement  in other words people who have damage to  this circuit will accept an immediate  reward but not a delayed one  think back to the example where the  child spent a small amount of money  right away rather than saving it to buy  something more expensive  the last circuit involves connections  between the amygdala the prefrontal  cortex and the orbital frontal cortex  this circuit is believed to be involved  in the regulation of our emotions  damage to this circuit could result in  the roller coaster ride of emotions  often noted in individuals with ADHD  there are four basic categories of  treatment for people with ADHD  medication  therapy  Education and Training and school-based  programs  keep in mind that many individuals  benefit benefit from involvement in all  four of these categories at the same  time  let's start by looking at medication  the first line of treatment medication  wise for individuals with ADHD is  stimulants  you might be thinking why would anyone  give a stimulant to someone who is  hyperactive  believe it or not they are pretty  effective in reducing hyperactivity and  impulsivity and improving one's ability  to focus work and learn  but how  stimulants tend to increase the  