ort from their families  and their teachers  Education and Training includes one  teaching parents the skills they need to  encourage and reward positive behaviors  in their children  two sharing stress management techniques  with parents so they can deal better  with their own frustrations and by  extension with their child's Behavior  and three having parents and families  join support groups so they can connect  with others who are dealing with similar  situations  the last category is school-based  programs  some schools offer special education  services to children with aedhd who  qualify  here education Specialists can help make  changes to classroom and homework  assignments in order to help the child  succeed  In Sum medication as well as a variety  of Support Services to help not only the  person with ADHD but also their families  are known to benefit individuals with  ADHD and maximize their best chances for  success  we've covered quite a bit in this  lecture  and I hope you now have a better  understanding of ADHD  join us in our next lecture as we  examine another disorder that is  frequently diagnosed in childhood  developmental dyslexia  bye for now

